---
<article class="border-l-4 border-[hsl(24,95%,53%)] pl-6">
  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-1">November 21, 2026</h2>
  <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mb-4">
    Added a plain-language explanation of how a breeder's records are protected: hourly backups kept far from
    where BreederHQ runs, locked so they cannot be deleted early, a daily copy with a second storage company,
    restores tested twice a week, and photos and documents copied as they are uploaded. The section also
    lists how long each kind of backup is kept and explains how to get a copy of your data.
  </p>

  <div class="mb-4">
    <h3 class="font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-1">Pages updated</h3>
    <ul class="text-sm text-gray-600 list-disc pl-5 space-y-1">
      <li><a href="/trust#your-data" class="text-[hsl(24,95%,53%)] hover:underline">/trust</a>: new "How We Keep Your Records Safe" section, plus two new FAQ entries ("Is my data backed up?" and "Can I get a copy of all my data?").</li>
      <li><a href="/faq" class="text-[hsl(24,95%,53%)] hover:underline">/faq</a>: new "Your Data" category with the same two questions.</li>
      <li><a href="/compare/breeders-assistant-alternative" class="text-[hsl(24,95%,53%)] hover:underline">/compare/breeders-assistant-alternative</a>: the "Data ownership" row now says what the backups and exports actually are.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</article>
